1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,260
The Marriage of Figaro, the whole story in short episodes. Episode one: the room next door.

2
00:00:05,580 --> 00:00:11,250
Near Seville, about 1786. Figaro, the Count's valet, marries Susanna, the Countess's maid, today.

3
00:00:11,570 --> 00:00:17,950
He is measuring their new bedroom, a gift from the Count. Perfect, says Figaro: if the Count rings at night, I'm there in two steps.

4
00:00:18,270 --> 00:00:23,650
Susanna is not charmed. And when the Count sends you away on an errand, she says, he's at my door in three steps.

5
00:00:23,970 --> 00:00:26,650
Because the Count, bored with his wife, now wants Susanna.

6
00:00:26,970 --> 00:00:35,080
He once abolished the old lord's right to a servant's bride. Now he regrets it, and wants it back from her. Her own singing teacher, Basilio, carries his messages.

7
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:42,530
Figaro sees the plan. The Count is going to London as ambassador: Figaro will be his courier, always away, with Susanna close at hand.

8
00:00:42,850 --> 00:00:49,740
So Figaro sings Se vuol ballare: if the Count wants to dance, I'll play the guitar. He will act the fool and turn every trick around.

9
00:00:50,060 --> 00:00:57,370
But Figaro has another enemy. Marcellina, the housekeeper, holds a paper with his signature. If it stands, Susanna is not the one he marries.

10
00:00:59,267 --> 00:01:01,997
The Marriage of Figaro, episode two: the contract.

11
00:01:02,317 --> 00:01:09,337
Marcellina, the palace housekeeper, once lent Figaro money. His signed promise: pay it back, or marry her. And today he marries Susanna.

12
00:01:09,657 --> 00:01:16,527
Her plan is clever: frighten Susanna into refusing the Count. The Count, offended, will take Marcellina's side, and Figaro will be hers.

13
00:01:16,847 --> 00:01:25,377
Her partner is old Doctor Bartolo. Why does he hate Figaro? In The Barber of Seville, Figaro helped the Count steal Bartolo's young ward, Rosina, who is now the Countess.

14
00:01:25,697 --> 00:01:33,147
So Bartolo sings La vendetta: revenge is a pleasure for the wise. He will search every law book for a trick, because all of Seville knows Bartolo.

15
00:01:33,467 --> 00:01:43,857
Then Marcellina meets Susanna in the doorway. A duel of curtsies: after you, my dazzling lady! No, after you, my spicy lady! Your position, says one. Your age, says the other. Marcellina storms off.

16
00:01:44,177 --> 00:01:51,367
Susanna is still laughing when someone rushes in: Cherubino, the Count's teenage page, in love with every woman in the palace. And he is in trouble.

17
00:01:53,267 --> 00:01:56,557
The Marriage of Figaro, episode three: the boy behind the chair.

18
00:01:56,877 --> 00:02:04,427
Yesterday the Count found Cherubino alone with Barbarina, the gardener's daughter, and sacked him. Now he begs Susanna: ask the Countess to save me.

19
00:02:04,747 --> 00:02:12,697
He adores the Countess. He snatches her ribbon from Susanna's hand and sings Non so più: I don't know what I am any more; every woman makes my heart race.

20
00:02:13,017 --> 00:02:20,187
Footsteps: the Count! Cherubino hides behind the big armchair. The Count sits, takes Susanna's hand and asks her to meet him in the garden at dusk.

21
00:02:20,507 --> 00:02:27,377
Then Basilio's voice outside. Now the Count hides behind the chair; the boy slips round onto the seat, and Susanna throws a dress over him.

22
00:02:27,697 --> 00:02:33,457
Basilio gossips: everyone knows the page is in love with the Countess. The Count jumps out. What does everyone say?

23
00:02:33,777 --> 00:02:40,437
Yesterday at Barbarina's, he says, I lifted the tablecloth, like this, and found the page! He lifts the dress. There is the page, again.

24
00:02:40,757 --> 00:02:44,417
Worse: the boy was there the whole time, and heard everything the Count said to Susanna.

25
00:02:46,167 --> 00:02:49,107
The Marriage of Figaro, episode four: off to the army.

26
00:02:49,427 --> 00:02:55,427
Figaro arrives with villagers dressed in white, throwing flowers: thank you, noble Count, for abolishing the old right!

27
00:02:55,747 --> 00:03:01,147
It's a trap. Figaro holds out a white veil: please, sir, put it on my bride yourself, here, in front of everyone.

28
00:03:01,467 --> 00:03:08,947
The Count can't refuse in public. He smiles, praises them, and asks for a little delay, for a grander ceremony. Quietly he adds: find Marcellina.

29
00:03:09,267 --> 00:03:15,057
And the page who heard too much? The Count forgives him, and makes him an officer in his regiment. He must leave at once.

30
00:03:15,377 --> 00:03:25,337
Figaro whispers to the boy: I must talk to you before you go. Then he teases him with Non più andrai: no more fluttering about, little butterfly. Now it's moustaches, muskets, and marching through the mud.

31
00:03:25,657 --> 00:03:30,217
But Cherubino is not leaving the palace. Upstairs, the Countess is alone and heartbroken.

32
00:03:31,967 --> 00:03:35,337
The Marriage of Figaro, episode five: the Countess's plan.

33
00:03:35,657 --> 00:03:44,467
Upstairs, the Countess is alone. Years ago the Count climbed balconies for her. Now he chases her maid. She sings Porgi, amor: love, give me back my husband, or let me die.

34
00:03:44,787 --> 00:03:53,257
Figaro has a plan. He has sent the Count an anonymous letter: tonight, during the dance, the Countess meets a lover. Let the jealous husband worry about his own wife for once.

35
00:03:53,577 --> 00:04:02,477
And Susanna will promise to meet the Count in the garden at dusk. But it won't be Susanna who goes. It will be Cherubino, in a dress, and the Countess will catch her husband in the act.

36
00:04:02,797 --> 00:04:11,067
The Count is out hunting, so there is time. Cherubino arrives and sings his song for the Countess, Voi che sapete: you ladies who know what love is, tell me, is this love?

37
00:04:11,387 --> 00:04:18,627
Susanna dresses him up: a lady's cap, eyes down, hands just so. The Countess notices that his officer's commission has no seal yet.

38
00:04:18,947 --> 00:04:24,877
Then, a knock. The Count is back early, with the letter. And in his wife's locked room stands a boy with half his clothes off.

39
00:04:26,767 --> 00:04:29,907
The Marriage of Figaro, episode six: the locked closet.

40
00:04:30,227 --> 00:04:38,757
Cherubino runs into the Countess's dressing closet. Pale, she lets her husband in. Why was the door locked? Then a crash from the closet: the boy has knocked over a chair.

41
00:04:39,077 --> 00:04:47,977
Who is in there? Only Susanna, says the Countess, trying on her wedding dress. In the trio Susanna, or via, sortite, the Count orders her to come out, and the Countess forbids it.

42
00:04:48,297 --> 00:04:55,337
The Count has had enough. He will break the door down. He locks every door, and takes his wife with him to fetch the tools, so nobody can slip away.

43
00:04:55,657 --> 00:05:03,947
But Susanna saw it all from the alcove. The moment they leave, she lets the boy out. The only way out is the window, above the gardener's flowerbeds. Cherubino jumps.

44
00:05:04,267 --> 00:05:06,877
Susanna locks herself in the closet in his place.

45
00:05:07,197 --> 00:05:14,337
The Count returns with a hammer and pliers. Now the Countess confesses: it's Cherubino, half undressed, but innocent, just a harmless joke.

46
00:05:14,657 --> 00:05:17,707
The Count snatches the key. Let him die! He turns to the door.

47
00:05:19,467 --> 00:05:22,517
The Marriage of Figaro, episode seven: the door opens.

48
00:05:22,837 --> 00:05:30,257
Out steps Susanna. Calm, smiling: my lord, why so surprised? The Count is lost. The Countess is just as stunned, but quickly plays along.

49
00:05:30,577 --> 00:05:38,387
Now the Count must beg forgiveness. Rosina, he says, her name from the old days. And the letter about a lover? Figaro wrote it, the women admit. Only a joke.

50
00:05:38,707 --> 00:05:48,627
Figaro bursts in: the music is ready, let's have the wedding! Then Antonio the gardener, Susanna's uncle, half drunk, with a smashed pot of carnations: a man jumped from this balcony onto my flowers!

51
00:05:48,947 --> 00:05:54,477
It was me, says Figaro, rubbing his ankle. Then you dropped this paper, says Antonio. The Count grabs it. What is it?

52
00:05:54,797 --> 00:06:01,257
The women whisper the answer: Cherubino's officer's commission. And why did you have it? Because, says Figaro, it needed the seal. Saved again.

53
00:06:01,577 --> 00:06:07,677
But then Marcellina, Bartolo and Basilio march in with the contract, and the Count smiles. He will judge the case himself.

54
00:06:09,567 --> 00:06:12,677
The Marriage of Figaro, episode eight: the trap in the garden.

55
00:06:12,997 --> 00:06:17,287
The Count paces. A locked closet, a letter, a jump from a window. Is he being played?

56
00:06:17,607 --> 00:06:27,037
The Countess has a new plan, and this one she keeps even from Figaro. Susanna will promise the Count a meeting in the garden tonight, but the Countess herself will go, in Susanna's clothes.

57
00:06:27,357 --> 00:06:37,177
Susanna finds the Count. Will she come? Yes, she says, if he gives her the dowry he promised, so she can pay off Marcellina. Their duet is Crudel, perché finora: cruel girl, why make me wait so long?

58
00:06:37,497 --> 00:06:41,847
He is delighted. But leaving, Susanna whispers to Figaro: you've already won your case.

59
00:06:42,167 --> 00:06:43,747
The Count hears it. A trap!

60
00:06:44,067 --> 00:06:50,207
In Vedrò mentr'io sospiro he rages: shall I sigh while my servant is happy? Never. Figaro will marry Marcellina.

61
00:06:50,527 --> 00:06:53,197
And the judge, Don Curzio, is ready with the verdict.

62
00:06:55,100 --> 00:06:57,450
The Marriage of Figaro, episode nine: Mother!

63
00:06:57,770 --> 00:07:02,330
The verdict: pay her or marry her. Two thousand silver pieces, and Figaro doesn't have them.

64
00:07:02,650 --> 00:07:12,290
One last trick: I'm a gentleman, he says. I can't marry without my noble parents' consent. Robbers stole me as a baby, dressed in gold, jewels and embroidery. And I have a mark on my arm.

65
00:07:12,610 --> 00:07:20,100
A little spatula, on the right arm? asks Marcellina. How do you know? Because you are my son, Raffaello. And your father is standing right there: Doctor Bartolo.

66
00:07:20,420 --> 00:07:25,120
Just then Susanna runs in with a purse: a thousand gold coins to set Figaro free.

67
00:07:25,440 --> 00:07:27,480
And she sees him hugging Marcellina.

68
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:28,700
Slap!

69
00:07:29,020 --> 00:07:29,830
Your mother?

70
00:07:30,750 --> 00:07:38,260
Yes, his mother! In the famous sextet everyone explains, Susanna laughs, and Marcellina and Bartolo decide to marry as well. Two weddings today.

71
00:07:38,580 --> 00:07:45,240
The Count leaves, beaten. But tonight his wife will wait for him in the garden in Susanna's dress, and Figaro knows nothing about it.

72
00:07:47,133 --> 00:07:50,163
The Marriage of Figaro, episode ten: the letter with the pin.

73
00:07:50,483 --> 00:07:56,473
The Countess, alone, remembers: Dove sono, where are the beautiful moments of sweetness and love? She will win her husband back.

74
00:07:56,793 --> 00:08:01,253
She dictates, Susanna writes, Sull'aria: what a gentle breeze tonight, under the pines.

75
00:08:01,573 --> 00:08:05,353
The letter is sealed with a pin; the Count must send the pin back as his answer.

76
00:08:05,673 --> 00:08:12,413
Village girls bring flowers to the Countess. Among them a shy one: Cherubino in a dress. Antonio pulls off the bonnet. Caught again!

77
00:08:12,733 --> 00:08:21,823
The Count wants to punish him, but Barbarina speaks up: you kissed me, sir, and promised me whatever I want. I want Cherubino as my husband. The Count is trapped by his own promises.

78
00:08:22,143 --> 00:08:31,503
The double wedding begins with a fandango. Kneeling for her bridal wreath, Susanna slips the Count the letter. He pricks his finger on the pin, drops it, then picks it up and pins it to his sleeve.

79
00:08:31,823 --> 00:08:36,993
Figaro sees and laughs: some girl has sent the Count a love note. He has no idea it was his bride.

80
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:41,950
The Marriage of Figaro, episode eleven: Figaro's jealousy.

81
00:08:42,270 --> 00:08:49,180
Night. Barbarina searches the garden with a lantern. She has lost the pin the Count gave her for Susanna, with a message: the seal of the pines.

82
00:08:49,500 --> 00:08:54,710
Figaro hears it, and his world falls apart. His bride, on their wedding day, has a meeting with the Count.

83
00:08:55,030 --> 00:09:03,820
Marcellina doubts it, but Figaro won't listen. He hides among the pines to catch them, and sings Aprite un po' quegli occhi: men, open your eyes and see what women really are.

84
00:09:04,140 --> 00:09:10,790
Susanna and the Countess arrive, already in each other's clothes. Marcellina has warned Susanna that Figaro is hiding nearby.

85
00:09:11,110 --> 00:09:20,410
So Susanna teases him. In Deh vieni, non tardar, one of the loveliest arias Mozart wrote, she sings: come, my love, don't be late. Figaro thinks it is for the Count. It is for him.

86
00:09:22,300 --> 00:09:25,500
The Marriage of Figaro, the last episode: Contessa, perdono.

87
00:09:25,820 --> 00:09:32,010
In the dark the Countess waits in Susanna's dress. Cherubino finds her, takes her for Susanna, and tries to steal a kiss.

88
00:09:32,330 --> 00:09:38,490
The Count steps between them and gets the kiss himself. He swings at the boy; the slap lands on Figaro, creeping closer.

89
00:09:38,810 --> 00:09:42,140
Then the Count woos "Susanna", really his own wife, and gives her a ring.

90
00:09:42,460 --> 00:09:48,310
Figaro meets "the Countess", but he knows that voice: it's Susanna. He plays along and declares his love to "my lady".

91
00:09:48,630 --> 00:09:49,530
Slap!

92
00:09:49,850 --> 00:09:51,380
Then they laugh and make up.

93
00:09:51,700 --> 00:09:58,270
The Count sees Figaro at the feet of "his wife" and explodes. He calls everyone out. Everyone begs: forgive! No, no, no, he shouts.

94
00:09:58,590 --> 00:10:00,530
Then the real Countess steps forward.

95
00:10:00,850 --> 00:10:07,210
The Count understands, and kneels: Contessa, perdono, Countess, forgive me. She does: I am kinder than you, and I say yes.

96
00:10:07,530 --> 00:10:10,990
The crazy day ends in a party. That was The Marriage of Figaro.
